problem:
Let $f$ be defined by  \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
3-x & \text{ if } x \leq 3, \\
-x^3+2x^2+3x & \text{ if } x>3.
\end{array}
\right.\]Calculate $f^{-1}(0)+f^{-1}(6)$.

target_step:
Now, I know that the probability of getting a sum of 7 is $\frac{47}{288}$, so I can set up an equation and solve for $x$:

$$
\frac{2}{36} - 2x^2 + \frac{4}{36} = \frac{47}{288}
$$

$$
-2x^2 = \frac{47}{288} - \frac{6}{36}
$$

$$
-2x^2 = \frac{47}{288} - \frac{72}{288}
$$

$$
-2x^2 = - \frac{25}{288}
$$

$$
x^2 = \frac{25}{576}
$$

$$
x = \frac{5}{24}
$$
